{"id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1", "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherds are cult leaders and agents within the Shepherd’s Flock—warped human figures guiding a fanatical movement—and they serve Maelthor, an otherworldly entity promising ascension through transformation and sacrifice.\n\nThe Shepherds are **leaders and religious figures** within the cult (the Shepherd’s Flock), described as **hardy humans warped by their discovery** and acting as recruiters, manipulators, and orchestrators of the cult’s spread. They present a **benevolent guise** while pursuing destructive goals like mass death, transformation, and rising “from below.” Their influence is both physical and psychological, described as being **“everywhere in the minds of the people.”**\n\nThey answer to **Maelthor**:\n- CANON: The cult’s beliefs explicitly state that **“The Shepherds are followers of Maelthor.”**\n- CANON: Maelthor is regarded as a **guardian of ancient, otherworldly wisdom and power**, promising **ascension and transcendence** to followers.\n- OBSERVED: The Shepherds justify atrocities (burnings, sacrifice, corruption) as necessary to advance **Maelthor’s influence** and a vision of human supremacy.\n\nThere is no conflicting attribution of their patron—Maelthor is consistently the power they serve across sources.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Demographics: Mostly disillusioned humans (veterans, laborers, apprentices)\n- Role: Cult leaders, recruiters, manipulators\n- History: Originated from human refugees; evolved into a fanatical cult\n- Goals: Death, transformation, rising from below, spreading influence\n- Alignment/Belief: Devotion to Maelthor; sacrifice and “purification” ideology", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 2069, "post_filter_count": 53, "duration_ms": 43, "top_5": [["ent_shepherd", 1.2442], ["ent_shepherds_flock", 1.1065], ["ent_seren_darkroot", 1.0], ["ent_great_shepherd", 0.9517], ["ent_maelthor", 0.8023]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_shepherd", "ent_shepherds_flock", "ent_seren_darkroot", "ent_great_shepherd", "ent_maelthor", "ent_leadership", "ent_maud", "ent_sing_enough_times_and_something_will_answer", "ent_human_refugees", "The_Shepherd_s_Council", "ent_secure_shipment_shepherds", "ent_ruined_altar", "ent_dead_gods_corrupted_flesh", "ent_gnome", "ent_stillness_as_power", "ent_peacemaker_fiddle", "ent_sepulcher", "ent_the_butcher", "ent_necrotic_planar_energy", "ent_abandoned_temple_of_nameless_god", "ent_nameless_god", "ent_political_intrigue_among_the_council", "ent_the_prophet", "ent_gilded_fold_calligraphy_stall", "ent_master_harrow", "Fey_stories_of_heroes_past", "ent_a_child_disappears_between_two_houses", "ent_changing_a_name_signals_a_life_transition", "ent_gods", "ent_jorren_coppermoss", "Kasrsemine", "Captain_Blart", "The_Protest", "Invisibility_Potion", "eldyrwyld", "ent_a_bridge_is_a_promise", "ent_a_whisper_promises_safety_through_control", "ent_abhorrent_meat_wings", "ent_a_predator_attacks_without_warning", "Hunter_s_Mark", "ent_message", "ent_elara_swiftwind", "ent_the_cult", "ent_servant_refectory", "ent_vane", "ent_city_guard", "ent_mayor", "ent_guardian", "ent_meat", "ent_hidden_tension", "ent_main_bridge", "ent_corrupted_meat", "ent_the_city"], "semantic_rerank": {"enabled": false}, "evidence_first": {"enabled": false}, "document_planner": {"enabled": false}, "projection_enriched": {"enabled": false}, "rich_entity_summaries": false}, "document_planner": {"enabled": false}, "context_chars": 30093, "duration_ms": 7467}
